#: views/settings.inc/config.tab.php:154
msgid ""
"The addresses that can get a device configuration over HTTP or HTTPS. Use "
"addresses or CIDR blocks, IPv4 or IPv6, separated by commas. Device "
"configurations contain SIP secrets, and phones cannot authenticate. Thus "
"this list is the only control of who can read them. An empty list refuses "
"all addresses. The module ignores this list when the Configuration Type is "
"File (TFTP/FTP)."
msgstr ""

#: views/settings.inc/config.tab.php:172
msgid "Trusted reverse proxies"
msgstr ""

#: views/settings.inc/config.tab.php:184
msgid ""
"Leave empty if phones do not reach this server through a reverse proxy. Use "
"the addresses or CIDR blocks of the proxies. For a request from these "
"addresses, the module uses the client address and scheme from X-Forwarded-"
"For and X-Forwarded-Proto. Thus the allowlist above applies to the phone and "
"not to the proxy, and HTTPS provisioning works when the proxy ends TLS. The "
"module ignores the forwarding headers of all other requests."
msgstr ""

